{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And they encamped beyond the Arnon.</b> Arnon is the name of the river, and they encamped on the far side of the river toward the land of Sihon, for they were going around the land of Moab, since they were not given permission to pass through its cities but only along its borders, as it is written: ״וגם אל מלך מואב שלח ולא אבה.״ And they came from the east, with the sun, to the land of Moab, and they left the land of Moab to the west, for they crossed beyond the Arnon toward the land of Sihon." "<b>For the Arnon is the boundary of Moab, between Moab and between the Amorite.</b> That is to say, the river separates between the two territories, for initially the entire land belonged to the king of Moab on both sides of the river, and Sihon took all that belonged to the king of Moab on the side of the Arnon, and from that war onward the river separated between the boundary of Moab and the boundary of the land of Sihon king of the Amorite. And that land across the Jordan River that Sihon conquered from Moab — Israel took from the hand of Sihon, as they said: Ammon and Moab were purified through Sihon — that is, they were purified and rendered fit for Israel by means of Sihon. And that territory the king of Ammon demanded from Israel, but it says: ״לא לקח ישראל מארץ מואב,״ for they did not cross the Arnon."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:44.948880722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}